TITLE:: RCUtil
summary:: Small pure utilities of the reCurrent module
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Guides/reCurrent

DESCRIPTION::
Key-value arrays ("kv") are flat arrays code::[key, value, key, value, ...]:: used wherever the order of pattern keys matters.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: rPut
METHOD:: rGet
Nested dictionary access by a key path.
METHOD:: kvAt
METHOD:: kvReplace
METHOD:: kvReplaceMany
METHOD:: kvPutAll
METHOD:: kvKeys
METHOD:: asKV
METHOD:: isStatic
True when a value can be used as-is in a pattern without being streamed.
METHOD:: cartesianProduct
Capped by link::#*maxProductSize::.
METHOD:: cartesianProductProducts
METHOD:: l1Vectors
The code::n::-dimensional integer vectors of L1 norm below code::t::, cached per code::(n, t):: and shared: iterate the result, never mutate it.
METHOD:: bagDifference
METHOD:: digitsInBase
METHOD:: fileTree
Folder → code::MultiLevelIdentityDictionary:: of PathNames.
METHOD:: attrFunc
A function-valued Event entry written code::{ }:: or code::{{ }}::.
METHOD:: camelCase
METHOD:: isReservedKey
True when code::ev.key:: would call a method instead of reading the key. The answer is cached per key (link::#*reservedKeyCache::): the scan of Event's method tables costs about 80 µs and is asked for every key of every beat created and at every attribute write.
METHOD:: reservedKeyCache
code::IdentityDictionary:: key → Boolean, reset by a class-library recompile.
METHOD:: warnIfReservedKey
METHOD:: maxProductSize
